# Plain "\n" line endings for every text file, on every computer. The pipeline
# writes its own files this way, and a file's hash (recorded in manifests and
# checked by helpers/audit.py) must not change just because Git rewrote its line
# endings on checkout. Git detects most binary files on its own; the kinds below
# are named so that Git never takes one for text (which would rewrite bytes that
# look like line endings, and corrupt the file).
* text=auto eol=lf

*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
